<title>JAPAN: Nippon Sanso shares inspired by firm earnings.</title>
<headline>Nippon Sanso shares inspired by firm earnings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Nippon Sanso Corp rose on Thursday morning, inspired by firm interim earnings results, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0043 GMT, the shares were 10 yen higher at 489 yen.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the oxygen maker said its parent current profit for the six months to September 30, 1996 was 2.08 billion yen, against 1.29 billion yen in the same period last business year.</p>
